WEBVTT

00:10.511 --> 00:12.679
[children shouting]

00:24.024 --> 00:25.317
[shouting stops]

00:27.528 --> 00:29.196
[girl] <i>This is a true story.</i>

00:30.364 --> 00:33.158
<i>It happened right here
in my town two years ago.</i>

00:34.451 --> 00:37.036
<i>A lot of people die
in a lot of really weird ways</i>

00:37.037 --> 00:38.412
<i>in this story,</i>

00:38.413 --> 00:39.956
<i>but you're not gonna find it
in the news</i>

00:39.957 --> 00:41.624
<i>or anywhere like that</i>

00:41.625 --> 00:44.836
<i>because the police and
the top people in this town</i>

00:44.837 --> 00:46.212
<i>were, like, so embarrassed</i>

00:46.213 --> 00:47.880
<i>that they weren't able
to solve it</i>

00:47.881 --> 00:49.925
<i>that they covered everything
all up.</i>

00:51.051 --> 00:53.511
<i>But if you come here
and ask anyone,</i>

00:53.512 --> 00:54.846
<i>they'll all tell you
the same thing</i>

00:54.847 --> 00:56.890
<i>that I'm gonna tell you now.</i>

00:58.100 --> 01:00.519
<i>This story starts
in my school.</i>

01:01.979 --> 01:03.354
<i>Maybrook Elementary</i>

01:03.355 --> 01:05.649
<i>is kindergarten
through fifth grade.</i>

01:07.401 --> 01:09.151
<i>So this one Wednesday</i>

01:09.152 --> 01:11.864
<i>is like a normal day
for the whole school.</i>

01:12.698 --> 01:15.617
<i>And they had this teacher
who was new.</i>

01:16.451 --> 01:19.121
<i>Her name was Justine Gandy.</i>

01:20.080 --> 01:22.957
<i>And on this day,
she was going to her classroom</i>

01:22.958 --> 01:24.543
<i>just like every morning.</i>

01:25.752 --> 01:27.713
<i>But today was different.</i>

01:28.672 --> 01:31.258
<i>Today, none of her kids
were there.</i>

01:32.676 --> 01:35.970
<i>Every other class at that
school had all their kids.</i>

01:35.971 --> 01:39.474
<i>Even the other third grade
Mrs. Belt taught was full.</i>

01:40.684 --> 01:43.937
<i>But Mrs. Gandy's room
was totally empty.</i>

01:45.564 --> 01:48.275
<i>Well, not totally.</i>

01:49.443 --> 01:51.152
<i>There was one boy there.</i>

01:51.153 --> 01:54.156
<i>And his name was Alex Lilly.</i>

01:54.907 --> 01:58.034
<i>And he was the only kid
in the class of 18</i>

01:58.035 --> 01:59.953
<i>that came to school that day.</i>

02:01.163 --> 02:02.539
<i>And do you know why?</i>

02:03.582 --> 02:05.375
<i>He was the only one there</i>

02:05.959 --> 02:09.879
<i>because the night before
at 2:17 in the morning,</i>

02:09.880 --> 02:13.090
<i>every other kid woke up,</i>

02:13.091 --> 02:14.510
<i>got out of bed,</i>

02:16.428 --> 02:17.846
<i>walked downstairs,</i>

02:19.306 --> 02:21.098
<i>opened the front door,</i>

02:21.099 --> 02:24.520
<i>walked across the front yard
and into the dark.</i>

02:25.479 --> 02:28.941
<i>And they never came back.</i>

02:29.691 --> 02:31.527
["Beware of Darkness" playing]

02:38.951 --> 02:40.701
<i>♪ Watch out now ♪</i>

02:40.702 --> 02:46.625
<i>♪ Take care
Beware of falling swingers ♪</i>

02:51.296 --> 02:54.299
<i>♪ Dropping all around you ♪</i>

02:58.720 --> 03:02.307
<i>♪ The pain
That often mingles ♪</i>

03:03.517 --> 03:10.232
<i>♪ In your fingertips ♪</i>

03:11.441 --> 03:15.529
<i>♪ Beware of darkness ♪</i>

03:22.452 --> 03:24.287
<i>♪ Watch out now ♪</i>

03:24.288 --> 03:30.210
<i>♪Take care
Beware of greedy leaders ♪</i>

03:34.673 --> 03:38.177
<i>♪ They take you
Where you should not go ♪</i>

03:42.264 --> 03:46.226
<i>♪ While weeping Atlas cedars ♪</i>

03:47.102 --> 03:50.981
<i>♪ They just want to grow ♪</i>

03:51.481 --> 03:54.276
<i>♪ Grow and grow ♪</i>

03:54.860 --> 03:58.155
<i>♪ Beware of darkness ♪</i>

03:58.655 --> 04:02.242
<i>♪ Beware of darkness... ♪</i>

04:10.000 --> 04:12.210
[girl] <i>All the parents
and people at the school</i>

04:12.211 --> 04:14.254
<i>were really sad and upset.</i>

04:15.589 --> 04:18.716
<i>The police could tell
that the kids left at 2:17</i>

04:19.468 --> 04:21.427
<i>because, like, half the houses
had alarms</i>

04:21.428 --> 04:23.764
<i>that got tripped
when they walked outside.</i>

04:27.267 --> 04:29.519
<i>Some of the kids
even got videoed</i>

04:29.520 --> 04:31.104
<i>by the houses
that had cameras.</i>

04:32.648 --> 04:34.482
<i>But the cameras
only showed the kids</i>

04:34.483 --> 04:36.443
<i>walking out into the darkness.</i>

04:38.445 --> 04:40.656
<i>They didn't show
where they went after that.</i>

04:43.492 --> 04:45.494
<i>The police talked
to Alex a lot.</i>

04:47.371 --> 04:50.331
<i>They asked him why his
classmates did what they did,</i>

04:50.332 --> 04:52.209
<i>but he told them
he didn't know.</i>

04:53.126 --> 04:55.211
<i>They asked him
if there was a plan,</i>

04:55.212 --> 04:57.506
<i>but he said if there was,
he never heard it.</i>

04:58.715 --> 05:00.633
<i>They asked him
if there was a TV show</i>

05:00.634 --> 05:02.427
<i>where someone ran away
like that,</i>

05:03.428 --> 05:05.889
<i>but he said if there was,
he never saw it.</i>

05:07.641 --> 05:10.393
<i>They also talked to Mrs. Gandy
a whole bunch,</i>

05:10.394 --> 05:12.103
<i>but she also
didn't know anything</i>

05:12.104 --> 05:13.355
<i>and couldn't help them.</i>

05:15.148 --> 05:16.357
<i>For almost a whole month,</i>

05:16.358 --> 05:19.319
<i>they kept the school closed
for their big investigation.</i>

05:21.029 --> 05:24.031
<i>But after a while, they had to
open everything back up,</i>

05:24.032 --> 05:27.327
<i>so that the kids that didn't
disappear could learn again.</i>

05:29.121 --> 05:30.913
<i>One night before they did,</i>

05:30.914 --> 05:33.166
<i>they had a big meeting
at the school.</i>

05:34.042 --> 05:35.293
<i>There was a bunch
of counselors</i>

05:35.294 --> 05:36.711
<i>and people like that</i>

05:36.712 --> 05:39.255
<i>to help everybody figure out
how to feel</i>

05:39.256 --> 05:41.592
<i>and be sad together, I guess.</i>

05:44.178 --> 05:46.597
<i>This is where the story
really starts.</i>

05:52.311 --> 05:55.438
[man] <i>What's important is
that we don't judge our grief.</i>

05:55.439 --> 05:57.982
We might experience emotions
we don't like.

05:57.983 --> 06:00.027
Emotions besides sadness.

06:00.986 --> 06:03.070
We need to make sure
that we allow ourselves

06:03.071 --> 06:05.157
to feel emotions like anger.

06:06.283 --> 06:10.037
Anger is a very healthy part
of the grief cycle.

06:10.579 --> 06:13.497
It can be especially powerful
in instances of abandonment.

06:13.498 --> 06:15.249
Now, there are often times
that we...

06:15.250 --> 06:16.792
[parent 1]
What does that mean?

06:16.793 --> 06:20.004
"Especially powerful
in instances of abandonment"?

06:20.005 --> 06:22.215
Are you saying that we should
be upset with Matthew?

06:22.216 --> 06:23.591
I'm saying it wouldn't
be abnormal...

06:23.592 --> 06:24.800
[parent 1]
I'll tell you right now

06:24.801 --> 06:26.552
that you may call
what happened "abandonment,"

06:26.553 --> 06:28.471
but I don't.
I don't see it like that.

06:28.472 --> 06:32.058
I see something that doesn't
make any sense at all.

06:32.059 --> 06:36.437
We're talking about 17 kids
in one classroom.

06:36.438 --> 06:38.272
What happened
in that classroom?

06:38.273 --> 06:41.025
Why just her classroom?
Why only hers?

06:41.026 --> 06:42.109
- [parent 2] Yeah!
- [others shout]

06:42.110 --> 06:43.569
[counselor] Look, I'm
picking up a lot of emotion,

06:43.570 --> 06:44.487
and that's fine.

06:44.488 --> 06:45.947
[parent 1] So you'll
forgive me if I'm not

06:45.948 --> 06:48.534
particularly interested in
hearing any more out of you.

06:49.076 --> 06:50.826
I wanna hear
from Justine Gandy.

06:50.827 --> 06:51.953
- [parent 2] Yeah.
- [others shout]

06:51.954 --> 06:54.163
[parent 1] She's here.
I wanna know exactly

06:54.164 --> 06:56.082
what she was doing in there.

06:56.083 --> 06:58.168
[overlapping shouting]

06:59.795 --> 07:01.088
[clears throat]

07:02.673 --> 07:03.674
Uh...

07:05.843 --> 07:07.218
I've...

07:07.219 --> 07:08.303
First...

07:10.097 --> 07:15.101
I just wanna say
how very sorry I am for...

07:15.102 --> 07:16.770
all of what's happened.

07:18.856 --> 07:22.860
I know there's nothing
I can say to make this better.

07:25.779 --> 07:27.864
The truth is,
is that I want an answer

07:27.865 --> 07:30.491
- just as bad as all of you.
- [parents shouting]

07:30.492 --> 07:32.827
- [parent 3] Finally. Liar!
- [parent 4] That bitch.

07:32.828 --> 07:34.036
I love those kids.

07:34.037 --> 07:35.121
[parents muttering]

07:35.122 --> 07:36.205
And...

07:36.206 --> 07:38.541
[parents shouting out]

07:38.542 --> 07:39.542
I... I know...

07:39.543 --> 07:41.294
[parent 5] We know you know
exactly what's going on.

07:41.295 --> 07:43.296
I know... I know it's...
it's not...

07:43.297 --> 07:45.631
She should be locked up until
she tells us what happened!

07:45.632 --> 07:47.176
[parents shouting]

07:48.093 --> 07:50.803
Okay, now that kind of thing
is really not called for.

07:50.804 --> 07:52.221
I'm serious.

07:52.222 --> 07:53.222
Mrs. Gandy is here

07:53.223 --> 07:55.516
as an affected member
of this community,

07:55.517 --> 07:56.726
and she is hurting
just like all of us.

07:56.727 --> 07:58.477
[parent 6] You're either
negligent or complicit!

07:58.478 --> 07:59.938
[parents shouting]

08:01.398 --> 08:03.816
[parent 7] Where are
our children, Mrs. Gandy?

08:03.817 --> 08:05.985
That's enough. Everybody needs
to give us some space.

08:05.986 --> 08:08.988
Please. Please.
It's been a long, long night.

08:08.989 --> 08:10.323
We need to get some sleep,

08:10.324 --> 08:12.241
wake up tomorrow
with clearer heads.

08:12.242 --> 08:13.826
[shouting continuing]

08:13.827 --> 08:15.620
Do you have anyone
you can stay with tonight?

08:15.621 --> 08:17.121
- Mm-mmm.
- Then I recommend you going

08:17.122 --> 08:18.539
straight home and laying low.

08:18.540 --> 08:20.292
This feels like
it could turn in...

08:26.465 --> 08:27.716
[person laughing nearby]

08:32.136 --> 08:33.554
[people chatting]

08:36.099 --> 08:37.892
Excuse me, ma'am,
I'm saving up for a bus ticket

08:37.893 --> 08:39.601
to see my brother. Do you have
any change on you at all?

08:39.602 --> 08:41.103
No, I'm sorry. Sorry.

08:41.104 --> 08:42.688
[music playing
through PA system]

09:16.306 --> 09:17.683
[phone buzzing]

09:24.231 --> 09:25.231
Hello?

09:25.232 --> 09:26.358
[heavy breathing on line]

09:27.484 --> 09:28.485
Hello?

09:29.278 --> 09:30.863
[heavy breathing continues]

09:32.239 --> 09:33.990
- Who is this?
<i>- You better watch your back</i>

09:33.991 --> 09:35.576
<i>because tonight's the
night that I...</i>

09:39.037 --> 09:40.621
Excuse me, miss,
I'm saving up for a bus ticket

09:40.622 --> 09:42.164
to see my brother.
Do you have any change?

09:42.165 --> 09:43.875
- No, sorry.
- Okay, thank you.

09:43.876 --> 09:45.878
[people chatting, shouting]

09:58.682 --> 10:00.142
[crickets chirping]

10:19.536 --> 10:20.996
- [bottles clinking]
- [bag thuds]

10:21.788 --> 10:22.873
[Justine exhales]

10:23.957 --> 10:25.709
[people chatting]

10:30.130 --> 10:31.423
[Justine sighs]

10:31.924 --> 10:35.010
<i>Anything the user does,
ZipString follows.</i>

10:35.719 --> 10:38.679
<i>The string flies
at around 35 miles per hour,</i>

10:38.680 --> 10:40.182
<i>and yet is safe to the touch.</i>

10:40.891 --> 10:44.603
<i>All right, Sharks, watch this
trick. It's called the swirl.</i>

10:46.897 --> 10:48.357
<i>This one's the corkscrew.</i>

10:48.982 --> 10:50.107
<i>This one's the step-through.</i>

10:50.108 --> 10:52.152
[doorbell rings]

10:52.653 --> 10:53.946
<i>And pop!</i>

10:54.738 --> 10:56.865
<i>Presenting the portal!</i>

10:59.868 --> 11:01.620
[Austin Hillam]
<i>ZipString glides...</i>

11:04.414 --> 11:05.457
Hello?

11:20.514 --> 11:21.515
Hello?

11:23.767 --> 11:25.060
Yes?

11:31.859 --> 11:33.068
[dog barking]

11:39.825 --> 11:41.743
- [dog barking]
- [Justine panting]

11:45.664 --> 11:46.915
[sighs]

11:51.044 --> 11:52.170
[pounding on door]

11:52.171 --> 11:54.131
- Jesus! Fucking what?
- [pounding stops]

11:57.384 --> 11:58.468
Who's there?

12:00.762 --> 12:01.763
Hello?

12:09.563 --> 12:10.564
Fuck!

12:15.569 --> 12:17.154
[dog barking]

12:39.301 --> 12:40.676
[children playing]

12:40.677 --> 12:42.428
[principal] <i>You're gonna keep
your health insurance,</i>

12:42.429 --> 12:44.264
and if you don't
mind me saying,

12:45.098 --> 12:47.767
there's a lot of mental health
specialists on the plan.

12:47.768 --> 12:48.809
Some of them are...

12:48.810 --> 12:51.854
I, uh...
I just need to work, you know?

12:51.855 --> 12:54.525
I just need to fill my days
with, uh...

12:56.235 --> 12:58.278
Yeah, I... I need to work.
So... [chuckles]

12:58.904 --> 13:01.447
Justine, the scene last night
was just proof

13:01.448 --> 13:04.076
that we have a lot
of emotional parents here.

13:04.701 --> 13:05.785
For now, I think it's best

13:05.786 --> 13:08.204
if you keep some distance
from this place

13:08.205 --> 13:11.123
until folks find time
to sort themselves out.

13:11.124 --> 13:12.918
[child screeching]

13:13.669 --> 13:15.002
How's Alex? Is he...

13:15.003 --> 13:16.420
Alex is doing well.

13:16.421 --> 13:19.382
He's in Mrs. Belt's class,
and we've been advised

13:19.383 --> 13:20.883
that the best thing
that we can do for him

13:20.884 --> 13:23.302
is keep him on a routine.
[inhales]

13:23.303 --> 13:25.304
Keep his life as normal
as possible.

13:25.305 --> 13:26.973
I would like to speak
with him.

13:26.974 --> 13:28.641
We've had this
conversation before.

13:28.642 --> 13:30.184
That's out of the question.

13:30.185 --> 13:32.061
Well, I would...
I would feel so much better

13:32.062 --> 13:33.479
if I could just
speak with him.

13:33.480 --> 13:34.939
- Right there.
- What?

13:34.940 --> 13:37.441
That's the problem.
You'd feel so much better.

13:37.442 --> 13:39.610
He's been scrutinized
by the press.

13:39.611 --> 13:42.029
He's had investigators
ransack his house.

13:42.030 --> 13:43.781
He's been traumatized.

13:43.782 --> 13:46.033
Let's try and put Alex
first, yes?

13:46.034 --> 13:48.536
If you're implying
that I don't care

13:48.537 --> 13:49.954
about Alex, or the students...

13:49.955 --> 13:52.331
The issue isn't you caring
or not caring.

13:52.332 --> 13:54.625
The issue here is,
you have a pattern

13:54.626 --> 13:56.627
in which you overstep
professional lines

13:56.628 --> 13:58.379
- with the students.
- Oh, my God. Here we go.

13:58.380 --> 13:59.463
You know, I do not overstep.

13:59.464 --> 14:01.883
You know it's not appropriate
to hug students.

14:01.884 --> 14:04.844
Oh, I hugged a crying
little boy. Lock me up.

14:04.845 --> 14:07.889
You know driving students home
is not professional.

14:07.890 --> 14:09.807
What? She missed the bus.
She lived close to me.

14:09.808 --> 14:11.185
- It's not appropriate.
- What...

14:11.977 --> 14:13.895
[sighs] I know all of this

14:13.896 --> 14:15.689
comes from the fact
that you care.

14:16.315 --> 14:18.733
I know that you aren't
a threat to these kids,

14:18.734 --> 14:20.234
but you have to realize,

14:20.235 --> 14:22.904
you aren't a parent,
you're a teacher.

14:22.905 --> 14:24.030
There's a difference.

14:24.031 --> 14:27.492
And for that reason, no,
you cannot talk to Alex Lilly.

14:31.705 --> 14:32.706
It's just...

14:34.875 --> 14:36.210
We're the only ones left.

14:39.046 --> 14:40.756
[people muttering]

14:43.967 --> 14:45.469
- No way.
- Look, look, look.

14:48.138 --> 14:49.139
[sniffles]

15:04.571 --> 15:05.447
[whimpers]

15:07.574 --> 15:09.368
Yeah, it's really
on there, huh?

15:10.327 --> 15:12.870
Yeah, I've been
receiving phone calls as well.

15:12.871 --> 15:14.330
- Threatening ones.
- Oh, yeah?

15:14.331 --> 15:16.917
Think the caller might be
responsible for this?

15:17.501 --> 15:19.961
I-I don't know.
Maybe, maybe not.

15:19.962 --> 15:20.879
Yeah, well...

15:21.421 --> 15:23.715
Whoever it was, the best
we can do is file a report.

15:24.508 --> 15:26.218
Probably kids did this,
if you ask me.

15:26.760 --> 15:27.593
I mean... [chuckles]

15:27.594 --> 15:28.886
...hell, I used to do
stuff like this

15:28.887 --> 15:30.304
when I was in school.

15:30.305 --> 15:33.140
You know, TP houses,
ding-dong ditch.

15:33.141 --> 15:34.767
I never wrote "witch"
on a car before,

15:34.768 --> 15:37.520
but a buddy of mine
smeared some of his own...

15:37.521 --> 15:39.815
["The Dark End of the Street"
playing]

15:53.120 --> 15:54.120
Hey!

15:54.121 --> 15:55.621
[both laugh]

15:55.622 --> 15:56.914
Can we hug?

15:56.915 --> 15:59.459
Yeah, of course we can hug.
Jesus.

16:09.052 --> 16:10.511
What happened
to your hand there?

16:10.512 --> 16:13.681
Oh, it was just a stupid
work accident thing.

16:13.682 --> 16:14.766
- Nothing.
- Drink?

16:15.517 --> 16:17.728
- Sure.
- Uh, Tony?

16:18.812 --> 16:19.812
Tony?

16:19.813 --> 16:21.689
Yeah, he'll...
he'll be here in a sec.

16:21.690 --> 16:23.191
- That's fine.
- So...

16:23.192 --> 16:24.484
- Yeah.
- I'm not in a rush.

16:24.985 --> 16:26.611
- [chuckles]
- Um...

16:26.612 --> 16:30.616
Wow. So I...
I didn't expect you to come.

16:32.326 --> 16:34.493
I'm glad you texted. I...

16:34.494 --> 16:37.413
You know, I've been thinking
about you a lot, and, uh...

16:37.414 --> 16:38.581
I wanted to call,

16:38.582 --> 16:42.043
but I didn't know if that
would make things worse or...

16:42.044 --> 16:43.419
- I don't know what's...
- Yeah, well,

16:43.420 --> 16:45.713
I'm not some
little delicate flower

16:45.714 --> 16:48.049
that would wilt if I saw your
name pop up on my phone.

16:48.050 --> 16:49.884
- I know. I'm not saying...
- So, yeah.

16:49.885 --> 16:52.887
Uh, Tony.
Uh, my friend wants a drink.

16:52.888 --> 16:54.139
Hi. Hi.

16:54.765 --> 16:57.391
- Uh, yeah. Go ahead.
- [Tony] How we doing?

16:57.392 --> 16:59.895
Hi. Um, I'll get a Coke.

17:01.146 --> 17:02.856
- A Coke?
- Yep.

17:05.233 --> 17:07.319
Okay, fine. Whatever.
[chuckles]

17:09.154 --> 17:10.739
So, what's going on?
How are you?

17:11.281 --> 17:13.534
Well, everybody thinks
I'm a witch.

17:14.867 --> 17:16.202
I don't think that's true.

17:16.203 --> 17:17.745
Go look at my car.

17:17.746 --> 17:20.040
Pfft.
I hope you didn't drive here.

17:20.582 --> 17:22.415
Why do you hope
that I didn't...

17:22.416 --> 17:24.043
I hope you didn't drive here
because...

17:24.044 --> 17:24.962
Wait...

17:26.421 --> 17:28.047
Don't be an asshole, Paul.

17:28.048 --> 17:29.131
- I'm not being an asshole.
- Come on.

17:29.132 --> 17:30.216
I'm not being an asshole.

17:30.217 --> 17:32.009
I'm concerned
about you, and...

17:32.010 --> 17:33.177
You know what? I don't need...

17:33.178 --> 17:35.847
I don't need
your fucking concern.

17:35.848 --> 17:37.598
Okay? I'm not drunk.

17:37.599 --> 17:39.434
Okay. Got it. I'm sorry.

17:45.274 --> 17:47.775
So what,
somebody vandalized your car?

17:47.776 --> 17:50.152
They wrote "witch" across it.
So, yes.

17:50.153 --> 17:52.822
For your information,
everybody thinks you're...

17:52.823 --> 17:55.116
I'm a witch.

17:55.117 --> 17:56.200
So, yes.

17:56.201 --> 17:57.786
- One Coke.
- Thank you.

18:05.210 --> 18:06.503
Can I give you a little, uh...

18:07.129 --> 18:08.963
- Tough love?
- No.

18:08.964 --> 18:10.423
Just some thoughts
from somebody

18:10.424 --> 18:11.842
who knows you very well.

18:13.886 --> 18:16.138
- Is that okay?
- Yep.

18:16.680 --> 18:19.766
Try to get out
of your own head.

18:21.101 --> 18:24.228
People are not all thinking
about you right now, okay?

18:24.229 --> 18:26.314
The whole town
isn't aimed at you.

18:26.315 --> 18:28.983
Hmm. I think you might
actually be wrong about that.

18:28.984 --> 18:32.653
You have a tendency
to get a little "woe is me"...

18:32.654 --> 18:35.990
- Wow. Wow. Okay.
- ...and a little paranoid.

18:35.991 --> 18:38.535
And one thing I know
has never helped is this.

18:40.370 --> 18:41.788
What is "this"? What?

18:43.790 --> 18:46.001
A lonely drinking pity party.

18:49.963 --> 18:51.089
I'm not lonely.

18:53.383 --> 18:54.468
You're here.

18:58.847 --> 19:01.808
You know what I mean, okay?
And I can't stay.

19:02.893 --> 19:04.228
Does Donna know you're here?

19:05.437 --> 19:06.270
No.

19:06.271 --> 19:07.980
- Really?
- Really.

19:07.981 --> 19:11.401
We're not... You know,
we're not happening right now.

19:13.195 --> 19:14.196
Wow.

19:16.490 --> 19:17.698
It's not a big deal.

19:17.699 --> 19:18.825
Mm-hmm.

19:21.954 --> 19:23.163
You're ridiculous.

19:23.747 --> 19:25.999
Look at you. You're beaming.

19:28.252 --> 19:30.086
Come on.
Have one real drink with me.

19:30.087 --> 19:32.339
- Justine, no. Justine.
- Come on. Please.

19:33.298 --> 19:34.466
Please?

19:36.760 --> 19:37.803
No.

19:38.804 --> 19:41.223
["Gotta Get Up" playing]

19:42.391 --> 19:44.433
<i>♪ Gotta get up
Gotta get out ♪</i>

19:44.434 --> 19:47.937
<i>♪ Gotta get home
Before the mornin' comes ♪</i>

19:47.938 --> 19:49.105
<i>♪ What if I'm late... ♪</i>

19:49.106 --> 19:50.731
Stop, please.

19:50.732 --> 19:51.691
[song continuing]

19:51.692 --> 19:53.318
You haven't changed a bit.

19:56.488 --> 19:58.031
What do you got
going on today?

19:58.532 --> 19:59.532
Work.

19:59.533 --> 20:02.076
Working. All day. Till late.

20:02.077 --> 20:04.579
Okay. I believe you. Jesus.

20:04.580 --> 20:05.913
What?

20:05.914 --> 20:07.164
Uh, don't-don't worry.

20:07.165 --> 20:08.958
I'm not gonna be, like,
spam texting you

20:08.959 --> 20:10.710
all day and night.
I learned my lesson.

20:10.711 --> 20:13.630
Justine, I'm just saying
I'm working. That's it.

20:16.592 --> 20:17.717
How's work?

20:17.718 --> 20:19.261
It's fine. It's whatever.

20:20.429 --> 20:23.765
Wow. I hope that's not
the general vibe over there.

20:24.474 --> 20:25.474
What does that mean?

20:25.475 --> 20:29.103
Well, there's 17
missing children out there,

20:29.104 --> 20:31.689
and I like to think the people
in charge of finding them

20:31.690 --> 20:34.150
aren't like, "Oh, whatever,"
about their jobs.

20:34.151 --> 20:36.110
First of all,
I'm not a detective.

20:36.111 --> 20:37.862
I don't know if you know that.

20:37.863 --> 20:40.364
Second of all,
I'm hungover as shit.

20:40.365 --> 20:43.242
I didn't realize I was getting
grilled on the investigation.

20:43.243 --> 20:44.368
[Justine] No, no, no.
I'm not...

20:44.369 --> 20:45.536
I'm not trying to grill.

20:45.537 --> 20:48.456
I'm just wondering if I need
to solve this thing myself.

20:48.457 --> 20:49.790
[Paul] We're on it.

20:49.791 --> 20:51.084
- You're on it?
- Yep.

20:52.252 --> 20:55.171
Okay, well, what a load off.

20:55.172 --> 20:56.256
You're on it.

20:57.257 --> 20:59.927
Right now, you really
need to take it easy.

21:00.469 --> 21:01.762
No one's slacking.

21:02.554 --> 21:03.971
Don't let yourself get all...

21:03.972 --> 21:05.598
Get all Justine about it?

21:05.599 --> 21:09.061
Just leave the investigating
to the investigators.

21:13.649 --> 21:14.983
It was great to see you.

21:16.068 --> 21:17.068
You too.

21:17.069 --> 21:18.570
[door handle clicking]

21:25.327 --> 21:26.870
Suck my dick.

22:10.581 --> 22:11.582
[chiming]

22:12.791 --> 22:14.251
[Justine patting her body]

22:22.843 --> 22:23.844
Hello?

23:04.593 --> 23:06.762
[crickets chirping]

23:11.225 --> 23:13.435
[flies buzzing]

23:55.894 --> 23:56.728
[gasps]

23:57.271 --> 23:58.355
[clanging]

24:12.160 --> 24:13.494
[principal]
<i>I explicitly told you</i>

24:13.495 --> 24:15.246
<i>not to interact with Alex.</i>

24:15.247 --> 24:17.123
Well, technically,
I didn't interact with him.

24:17.124 --> 24:18.457
<i>You followed him home.</i>

24:18.458 --> 24:20.543
<i>You rang his doorbell
repeatedly</i>

24:20.544 --> 24:22.336
<i>then spied through a window.</i>

24:22.337 --> 24:24.422
Well, can... can we
just focus on the fact

24:24.423 --> 24:25.923
that that house is bizarre?

24:25.924 --> 24:28.176
<i>Justine, if I wasn't clear
with you before,</i>

24:28.177 --> 24:29.886
<i>let me do so now.</i>

24:29.887 --> 24:32.597
<i>I want you to leave him alone.</i>

24:32.598 --> 24:34.515
Okay, why were his windows
taped up?

24:34.516 --> 24:36.142
Doesn't that seem strange
to you?

24:36.143 --> 24:38.811
<i>Probably because nosy people
take it upon themselves</i>

24:38.812 --> 24:40.271
<i>to walk up
and peek through them.</i>

24:40.272 --> 24:41.940
- But, Marcus...
- <i>Are you kidding?</i>

24:42.900 --> 24:44.358
<i>I'm gonna do you the courtesy</i>

24:44.359 --> 24:47.070
<i>of forgetting that this
phone call ever took place.</i>

24:47.738 --> 24:48.946
[door beeps]

24:48.947 --> 24:50.866
[music playing
through PA system]

25:13.889 --> 25:14.889
[Justine shrieks]

25:14.890 --> 25:16.307
[grunts]

25:16.308 --> 25:18.267
- What the fuck?
- You fucked him?

25:18.268 --> 25:19.394
Donna?

25:19.937 --> 25:21.479
- You fucked him?
- Donna, no. I...

25:21.480 --> 25:22.605
I-I didn't fuck him.

25:22.606 --> 25:24.690
- Yes, you did. I know you did.
- No, no, no. No, he...

25:24.691 --> 25:26.442
He said you weren't together.

25:26.443 --> 25:27.527
- Liar!
- No, no, no!

25:27.528 --> 25:29.445
- You got him drunk!
- Donna, stop. Stop!

25:29.446 --> 25:32.490
He was trying to be nice
to you, and you got him drunk!

25:32.491 --> 25:33.824
- Hey! Hey! Don't!
- Stop!

25:33.825 --> 25:35.284
[Donna] Look at what you did!

25:35.285 --> 25:37.204
Look at what you did!

25:37.955 --> 25:40.873
[woman on TV] <i>Luciano, I know
we got off to a rocky start</i>

25:40.874 --> 25:43.584
<i>with everything that happened
in the Jacuzzi,</i>

25:43.585 --> 25:45.754
<i>but still you have made me...</i>

26:00.769 --> 26:02.771
[clock ticking]

26:13.365 --> 26:15.242
[ticking continues]

27:04.833 --> 27:05.917
[gasps]

27:05.918 --> 27:07.835
[panting]

27:07.836 --> 27:09.171
[clock ticking]

27:10.172 --> 27:11.381
[muffled thudding]

27:39.618 --> 27:41.245
[screaming]

27:45.249 --> 27:47.251
[panting]

27:47.793 --> 27:48.794
Oh, my God.

27:56.927 --> 27:59.471
Alex, hi. How are you?

28:02.057 --> 28:03.599
I-I just wanted to say hi

28:03.600 --> 28:06.728
'cause I've been thinking
about you a lot, and...

28:07.354 --> 28:08.563
I wanted to make sure
you're okay.

28:08.564 --> 28:09.731
I'm okay.

28:11.817 --> 28:12.859
Yeah?

28:12.860 --> 28:17.864
'Cause I know it's been
a really hard time for me,

28:17.865 --> 28:20.867
and I can't even imagine
how it's been like...

28:20.868 --> 28:21.952
I have to go.

28:22.953 --> 28:24.787
Hey, hang on, please.

28:24.788 --> 28:26.497
I just...
I just want to make sure

28:26.498 --> 28:28.542
- that everything's all right.
- Don't follow me!

28:36.008 --> 28:38.844
Hello? It's Ms. Gandy.
I'd like to talk to you.

28:43.265 --> 28:44.266
Hello?

28:47.728 --> 28:49.021
I know you're home.

28:49.605 --> 28:51.231
[crickets chirping]

30:40.090 --> 30:41.383
[door opening]

30:51.351 --> 30:52.477
[snipping]

31:08.327 --> 31:09.453
[heavy breathing]

31:40.734 --> 31:41.735
I'm going to work.

32:06.969 --> 32:08.387
[keyboard clacks]

32:37.791 --> 32:38.791
[clears throat]

32:38.792 --> 32:40.502
[hammering]

32:41.003 --> 32:42.420
Been calling you
all morning, boss.

32:42.421 --> 32:44.338
Yeah, I hit a snag
on the way over.

32:44.339 --> 32:45.757
[machinery whirring]

32:47.509 --> 32:48.551
How things looking?

32:48.552 --> 32:50.596
[chuckles] Little bit
of a chaotic morning.

32:51.180 --> 32:52.431
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

32:53.098 --> 32:54.640
Marc went to go pick up
the sodding,

32:54.641 --> 32:55.766
but they didn't have it in

32:55.767 --> 32:57.476
'cause the order
never got placed.

32:57.477 --> 32:59.855
Shit. Goddamn it. That...

33:00.772 --> 33:02.231
All right,
I'm sorry about that.

33:02.232 --> 33:04.984
Yeah, we got the owner coming
Friday for a walk-through,

33:04.985 --> 33:07.111
and we're still gonna
have the open frame in.

33:07.112 --> 33:08.447
It's on me. It's my bad.

33:09.114 --> 33:10.948
And then I showed up,
and I see that Alvin

33:10.949 --> 33:13.493
painted the door with the
paint that you ordered, and...

33:14.203 --> 33:15.204
Yeah?

33:15.871 --> 33:17.664
They wanted forest green
and that's red.

33:18.665 --> 33:19.874
- What?
- Look.

33:19.875 --> 33:21.918
Goddamn it. Wait a minute.
Did they send the wrong...

33:21.919 --> 33:23.878
I checked the order,
and we ordered it.

33:23.879 --> 33:25.838
They sent what we asked for,
but what we asked for was...

33:25.839 --> 33:27.590
All right. I fucked up.

33:27.591 --> 33:29.676
I'll take it back,
get the right one.

33:36.808 --> 33:38.310
[low chatter]

33:46.693 --> 33:47.694
Mr. Graff.

33:48.570 --> 33:49.571
Yeah.

33:51.365 --> 33:53.449
We follow up on
every one of these calls.

33:53.450 --> 33:55.201
So I can assure you
that as we speak,

33:55.202 --> 33:57.119
we have officers
aggressively pursuing

33:57.120 --> 33:59.122
every lead that comes
through this station.

33:59.623 --> 34:01.499
So, what about the feds?
They got nothing new?

34:01.500 --> 34:04.252
There continues to be a very
healthy information exchange.

34:04.253 --> 34:06.003
So I can tell you
with full confidence

34:06.004 --> 34:09.049
that they are also pursuing
every lead aggressively.

34:10.342 --> 34:11.801
What's happening
with the K-9 units?

34:11.802 --> 34:14.428
I haven't heard about any
K-9 reports in a long time.

34:14.429 --> 34:16.514
That's because
they don't report to you.

34:18.684 --> 34:20.977
Mr. Graff, I can understand
your passion.

34:20.978 --> 34:23.145
And I don't mind having
these conversations with you

34:23.146 --> 34:24.939
because, God forbid,
if it was my child,

34:24.940 --> 34:26.482
I'd be demanding answers too.

34:26.483 --> 34:29.068
But I need you to trust
that what we're doing here...

34:29.069 --> 34:30.529
She's still not talking, huh?

34:33.447 --> 34:34.449
She knows.

34:34.949 --> 34:36.618
I disagree with that.

34:37.369 --> 34:39.995
You're aggressively
following up on every lead,

34:39.996 --> 34:43.374
and yet she's just out there
walking around free as a bird.

34:43.375 --> 34:45.751
Have you done any looking
into her whatsoever?

34:45.752 --> 34:47.253
Extensively. Yes, we have.

34:47.254 --> 34:48.629
So you know about
her past, huh?

34:48.630 --> 34:50.299
'Cause I've done some digging.

34:50.882 --> 34:52.467
And I've found out a lot.

34:53.092 --> 34:56.345
She had a DUI two years ago.
Did you not see that?

34:56.346 --> 34:58.848
She was let go from her
last school that she taught at

34:58.849 --> 35:00.099
for inappropriate behavior.

35:00.100 --> 35:01.601
Did you not see
that one either?

35:01.602 --> 35:03.895
With a member of the faculty.

35:03.896 --> 35:06.148
She's a troubled person,
is she not?

35:08.275 --> 35:10.027
What is it you think
that she knows?

35:11.695 --> 35:13.654
What do you think it is
that she's not telling us?

35:13.655 --> 35:15.406
Because those kids walked out
of those homes.

35:15.407 --> 35:16.700
No one pulled them out.

35:17.826 --> 35:19.285
No one forced them.

35:19.286 --> 35:20.953
I don't see
anything whatsoever

35:20.954 --> 35:22.623
that points to that woman.

35:25.459 --> 35:27.044
What do you see that I don't?

35:27.836 --> 35:30.546
I see something that
I don't understand at all.

35:30.547 --> 35:31.631
[parent 1] Yeah!

35:31.632 --> 35:35.635
We're talking about 17 kids
in one classroom.

35:35.636 --> 35:37.094
And none of them
talked about it?

35:37.095 --> 35:38.054
[parent 2] Exactly.

35:38.055 --> 35:39.555
And we got how many parents
in here,

35:39.556 --> 35:41.224
and none of us saw it coming?

35:41.225 --> 35:42.767
[parents shouting]

35:42.768 --> 35:45.561
I want to know what happened
in that classroom.

35:45.562 --> 35:48.189
Why just her classroom?
Why only hers?

35:48.190 --> 35:50.441
[overlapping voices]

35:50.442 --> 35:51.817
[parent 3]
Where are our children?

35:51.818 --> 35:52.985
[parent 4]
You're just gonna leave?

35:52.986 --> 35:53.903
[Marcus] That's enough.

35:53.904 --> 35:55.196
Everybody needs to give us
some space.

35:55.197 --> 35:56.698
- Please. Please.
- [shouting continuing]

35:57.241 --> 35:59.242
Let's all get
a good night's sleep.

35:59.243 --> 36:00.911
Wake up with clearer heads.
Please.

36:02.579 --> 36:04.373
- [parent 5] She has answers!
- [parents shouting]

36:09.962 --> 36:11.504
Excuse me, miss, I'm saving up
for a bus ticket

36:11.505 --> 36:13.089
to see my brother. Do you have
any change on you at all?

36:13.090 --> 36:14.216
[Justine] Sorry.

36:47.082 --> 36:48.083
[gasps]

37:19.323 --> 37:20.324
Matthew?

37:35.297 --> 37:36.298
Matthew.

37:38.383 --> 37:39.426
[hinge squeaks]

37:41.845 --> 37:43.055
[panting]

37:49.102 --> 37:50.229
Matthew!

37:53.357 --> 37:54.358
Stop!

38:16.380 --> 38:17.381
Wait.

38:30.853 --> 38:32.271
[thunder rumbles]

38:57.629 --> 38:59.756
[footsteps running up stairs]

39:28.076 --> 39:29.077
Matthew?

40:07.449 --> 40:08.450
Matthew?

40:10.661 --> 40:12.079
[gasps]

40:16.917 --> 40:18.252
Matthew, where are you?

40:22.381 --> 40:23.799
Where did you go?

40:28.679 --> 40:29.680
Talk to me.

40:31.431 --> 40:32.599
Talk to me!

40:39.189 --> 40:40.524
[sniffs, groans]

40:41.817 --> 40:42.860
I'm sorry.

40:44.361 --> 40:46.488
I'm sorry that
I wasn't able to sa...

40:47.739 --> 40:48.949
That I wasn't able...

40:53.537 --> 40:55.789
I wanted to say it
so many times.

40:58.417 --> 41:00.168
I really do want to say it
all the time

41:00.169 --> 41:02.588
because I feel it
all the time.

41:08.468 --> 41:09.595
I love you so much.

41:10.721 --> 41:11.721
[shouts]

41:11.722 --> 41:13.473
[grunting, panting]

41:19.813 --> 41:20.981
What the fuck?

41:51.595 --> 41:53.055
Where's our house?

41:54.097 --> 41:55.390
There.

42:01.480 --> 42:05.441
Where's the tower? Tower,
tower, tower, tower, tower.

42:05.442 --> 42:06.860
Ah.

42:21.416 --> 42:22.417
Show me.

42:24.837 --> 42:25.838
Come on.

42:33.595 --> 42:34.805
[bell chiming]

42:42.479 --> 42:43.604
Hi.

42:43.605 --> 42:45.148
- Hello.
- How are you?

42:46.692 --> 42:47.859
I'm Archer Graff.
I'm Matthew's...

42:47.860 --> 42:49.318
Yeah, I know who you are. Hi.

42:49.319 --> 42:52.406
Oh, good. I know we haven't
spoken before directly.

42:53.073 --> 42:54.949
We've seen each other
at a lot of the same...

42:54.950 --> 42:57.578
- How are you, Archer?
- I'm good. I'm real good.

42:58.370 --> 42:59.662
I... You know.

42:59.663 --> 43:01.707
All things considered, just...

43:03.000 --> 43:04.459
soldiering on.

43:05.377 --> 43:06.712
We have to, don't we?

43:07.212 --> 43:08.212
We do.

43:08.213 --> 43:11.299
Listen, I'm sorry to
surprise you at home like this

43:11.300 --> 43:12.800
in the...
in the middle of the day.

43:12.801 --> 43:14.760
But, um, I don't know
if you know,

43:14.761 --> 43:16.971
but we got some footage of
Matthew leaving the house

43:16.972 --> 43:18.891
on our Ring cam thing here,

43:19.725 --> 43:21.894
and I think you folks
had the same...

43:22.436 --> 43:23.979
same situation with Bailey?

43:24.688 --> 43:25.855
Yeah, that's right.

43:25.856 --> 43:28.065
All right. Well, I'm sure
you showed yours to the police

43:28.066 --> 43:30.194
just like I did, but I-I...

43:31.236 --> 43:34.198
I wondered if you would mind
letting me take a look at it.

43:35.032 --> 43:36.157
I don't need a copy
or anything.

43:36.158 --> 43:37.618
I'm not comfortable with that.

43:42.956 --> 43:44.458
Okay. I understand.

44:06.897 --> 44:07.898
Gary?

44:08.899 --> 44:10.275
Archer Graff. How you doing?

44:10.943 --> 44:11.944
Fine.

44:12.653 --> 44:13.946
Matthew's dad.

44:14.947 --> 44:17.032
Yeah. [sighs] Of course.

44:18.116 --> 44:19.116
How's it going?

44:19.117 --> 44:21.954
Um, I have a strange question
I need to ask you.

44:26.667 --> 44:28.209
It's kinda hard to watch this.

44:28.210 --> 44:30.044
Okay, wait. Go back to where
she steps on the sidewalk.

44:30.045 --> 44:31.128
Okay.

44:31.129 --> 44:32.214
Uh...

44:33.006 --> 44:34.925
Okay. Right there.

44:36.426 --> 44:37.469
[Gary] What do you see?

44:39.096 --> 44:41.597
One, two, three, four...

44:41.598 --> 44:45.143
...five, six, seven.

44:59.366 --> 45:00.450
Sorry.

45:20.888 --> 45:22.556
Come on. What am I looking at?

45:57.382 --> 45:58.383
Hey.

45:59.176 --> 46:00.801
- I want to talk to you.
- Well, I...

46:00.802 --> 46:02.762
I don't think we have anything
to say to each other.

46:02.763 --> 46:03.888
