01:08:13.760 --> 01:08:16.344
"What'd I tell you, huh?
What'd I tell you?

01:08:16.345 --> 01:08:18.515
What'd I tell you?
I'm a big cop, and I..."

01:08:21.100 --> 01:08:21.935
[gasps]

01:08:25.314 --> 01:08:27.149
[crickets chirping]

01:08:50.714 --> 01:08:52.006
[panting]

01:08:59.096 --> 01:09:00.681
You're okay. You're okay.

01:09:00.682 --> 01:09:02.683
That wasn't real. That wasn't
real. That wasn't real.

01:09:02.684 --> 01:09:04.019
- It's okay. You're okay.
- [twig snaps]

01:09:07.356 --> 01:09:08.774
[James panting]

01:09:28.877 --> 01:09:30.921
[James panting]

01:09:33.590 --> 01:09:34.883
[Paul screams]

01:09:35.843 --> 01:09:36.844
[James] Fuck.

01:09:40.013 --> 01:09:41.681
Fucker! You stabbed me!

01:09:41.682 --> 01:09:43.516
No, no, no. I'm sorry.
Sorry. It was an accident.

01:09:43.517 --> 01:09:44.934
It was an accident. I'm sorry.

01:09:44.935 --> 01:09:46.644
Wait, wait, wait. Wait, wait.
Wait, wait.

01:09:46.645 --> 01:09:47.728
I know where those kids are.

01:09:47.729 --> 01:09:48.980
That's why I was coming
to the station.

01:09:48.981 --> 01:09:50.940
- You're fucking lying!
- No, no, no, I'm not. I'm not.

01:09:50.941 --> 01:09:53.067
I promise. I promise. I know
where they are. I promise.

01:09:53.068 --> 01:09:54.110
Where?

01:09:54.111 --> 01:09:55.152
[stammering]

01:09:55.153 --> 01:09:57.989
They're at-at-at a house,
not far, in the basement.

01:09:57.990 --> 01:10:00.033
What the fuck are you t...
What house?

01:10:00.659 --> 01:10:01.826
I... I can show you, man.

01:10:01.827 --> 01:10:03.579
It's-it's really, really,
really close.

01:10:17.259 --> 01:10:18.844
Oh, fuck me.

01:10:21.054 --> 01:10:22.055
Do you have AIDS?

01:10:23.515 --> 01:10:24.515
Huh?

01:10:24.516 --> 01:10:26.894
AIDS, asshole.
Do you have AIDS?

01:10:27.436 --> 01:10:28.728
Uh...

01:10:28.729 --> 01:10:30.314
Uh, I don't think so.

01:10:30.814 --> 01:10:32.274
Hepatitis? Shit like that?

01:10:33.066 --> 01:10:35.110
I mean, shit,
not that I know of.

01:10:45.579 --> 01:10:46.621
That one, the dark one.

01:10:46.622 --> 01:10:47.998
Right there
at the end of the block.

01:11:01.970 --> 01:11:03.387
Um, excuse me, sir.

01:11:03.388 --> 01:11:05.349
Um, I don't want to be rude,
but, like,

01:11:05.933 --> 01:11:07.475
how do I know you aren't
gonna try and, like,

01:11:07.476 --> 01:11:09.311
take that reward for yourself?

01:11:12.689 --> 01:11:13.690
Sir?

01:11:15.859 --> 01:11:16.860
Sir?

01:11:17.986 --> 01:11:18.987
Officer?

01:11:20.614 --> 01:11:22.574
Oh, man.

01:11:37.422 --> 01:11:38.966
[no audible dialogue]

01:11:41.385 --> 01:11:42.553
[mouthing words]
What the fuck?

01:11:52.771 --> 01:11:53.939
What the fuck?

01:11:54.606 --> 01:11:55.606
[crickets chirping]

01:11:55.607 --> 01:11:57.734
What the fuck? [groans]

01:11:59.152 --> 01:12:02.406
Let me the fuck out of here.
Goddamn it.

01:12:05.617 --> 01:12:07.661
Oh. Thank you.

01:12:13.166 --> 01:12:14.334
[whispering] What the fuck?

01:12:22.509 --> 01:12:25.303
Jesus Christ. What the fuck?
Hey, yo, you good?

01:12:25.304 --> 01:12:26.470
- [Paul snarling]
- Jesus Christ, bro!

01:12:26.471 --> 01:12:28.306
- Hey! Get off me, bro!
- [Paul growls]

01:12:28.307 --> 01:12:31.392
Get the fuck off me!
Get the fuck off me!

01:12:31.393 --> 01:12:32.727
Hey! Fuck!

01:12:32.728 --> 01:12:35.522
Help me! Help me!
Someone, please help me!

01:12:40.694 --> 01:12:42.904
[Justine] <i>I'm telling you,
Marcus. I've seen it myself.</i>

01:12:42.905 --> 01:12:45.656
<i>There's something
very, very wrong</i>

01:12:45.657 --> 01:12:47.033
<i>going on inside of that house.</i>

01:12:47.034 --> 01:12:48.117
<i>If you don't believe me,</i>

01:12:48.118 --> 01:12:49.368
<i>- go there yourself.</i>
- Justine, stop.

01:12:49.369 --> 01:12:50.828
Here's the bottom line.

01:12:50.829 --> 01:12:52.330
Alex has been
traumatized enough

01:12:52.331 --> 01:12:54.498
by the events
of the last two months,

01:12:54.499 --> 01:12:56.667
- as I'm sure you have.
<i>- Marcus...</i>

01:12:56.668 --> 01:12:58.961
Which is why I'm gonna do
you the courtesy

01:12:58.962 --> 01:13:01.005
of forgetting that this
phone call ever took place.

01:13:01.006 --> 01:13:04.467
<i>If a child's welfare
is questioned, by law...</i>

01:13:04.468 --> 01:13:05.635
- Justine.
<i>- ...you have to refer it</i>

01:13:05.636 --> 01:13:07.220
<i>to CPS.</i>

01:13:07.221 --> 01:13:08.304
<i>By law.</i>

01:13:08.305 --> 01:13:09.806
Are you really gonna
take it there?

01:13:10.807 --> 01:13:12.391
Is this the corner
you're gonna put me in?

01:13:12.392 --> 01:13:14.810
<i>Just go make the house call,
Marcus. Just do that.</i>

01:13:14.811 --> 01:13:18.648
I'm not authorized
to just make house calls.

01:13:18.649 --> 01:13:20.776
<i>Well, you're a mandatory
reporter. You have to.</i>

01:13:21.485 --> 01:13:22.652
Okay, here's what I'll do.

01:13:22.653 --> 01:13:25.696
I'll invite his parents to
come in, have a talk with me.

01:13:25.697 --> 01:13:28.241
We'll have a face-to-face
at the school.

01:13:28.242 --> 01:13:29.951
Is that acceptable to you?

01:13:29.952 --> 01:13:32.537
<i>Yes, thank you. I would
really appreciate that.</i>

01:13:32.538 --> 01:13:35.082
Okay, then. You're welcome.
Goodbye.

01:13:37.543 --> 01:13:39.336
- [knocking at door]
- Yeah.

01:13:42.172 --> 01:13:43.714
Your two o'clock is here.

01:13:43.715 --> 01:13:44.925
That's fine.

01:13:48.554 --> 01:13:51.348
Well, send them in, please,
Marge.

01:13:53.976 --> 01:13:55.143
This way, ma'am.

01:14:08.740 --> 01:14:11.285
Principal Miller, I'm Gladys.

01:14:12.369 --> 01:14:14.496
Yes. H-Hi. Hi.

01:14:15.038 --> 01:14:16.039
Come on in.

01:14:16.790 --> 01:14:19.334
- Have a seat, please.
- Oh, thank you.

01:14:25.174 --> 01:14:26.175
Thank you, Marge.

01:14:30.470 --> 01:14:32.806
Thank you for coming in. I...

01:14:33.432 --> 01:14:36.142
I know you guys have had
a lot of attention lately.

01:14:36.143 --> 01:14:38.769
Not all of it
could possibly be wanted.

01:14:38.770 --> 01:14:41.147
I'm happy to come by.
It's fine.

01:14:41.148 --> 01:14:42.940
Okay. Forgive me...

01:14:42.941 --> 01:14:44.860
We have not met.
Is that right?

01:14:45.569 --> 01:14:46.944
No, I don't think so.

01:14:46.945 --> 01:14:48.571
- Okay... Phew.
- [Gladys laughs]

01:14:48.572 --> 01:14:52.242
Because I was relatively
certain I'd remember.

01:14:52.910 --> 01:14:55.286
I know I've met
Alex's father before.

01:14:55.287 --> 01:14:56.913
I'm Alex's aunt,

01:14:56.914 --> 01:14:58.497
and his mom's my baby sister.

01:14:58.498 --> 01:15:01.834
Okay. So you're not
his legal guardian.

01:15:01.835 --> 01:15:04.504
Well, no. That would be
his parents, of course.

01:15:04.505 --> 01:15:06.839
Okay. Well, uh...

01:15:06.840 --> 01:15:07.924
Forgive me, Gladys,

01:15:07.925 --> 01:15:11.886
but unfortunately, I need
to speak with his parents.

01:15:11.887 --> 01:15:13.347
[sighs]

01:15:13.847 --> 01:15:15.848
Well, I hate to say it,

01:15:15.849 --> 01:15:18.809
but his parents have been
feeling unwell as of late,

01:15:18.810 --> 01:15:21.687
and I'm staying with them
to help take care of Alex.

01:15:21.688 --> 01:15:23.565
Oh. S-Sounds serious.

01:15:24.233 --> 01:15:26.400
Oh, no. No, it's not serious.
Nothing terminal.

01:15:26.401 --> 01:15:28.027
It's just a touch
of consumption.

01:15:28.028 --> 01:15:29.655
"A touch of consumption"?

01:15:30.322 --> 01:15:31.156
Yeah.

01:15:31.990 --> 01:15:33.324
You know what?

01:15:33.325 --> 01:15:34.492
I'm embarrassed to say

01:15:34.493 --> 01:15:36.912
I guess I don't really know
what that means.

01:15:37.412 --> 01:15:38.412
I thought it was something

01:15:38.413 --> 01:15:40.248
settlers got
on the Oregon Trail.

01:15:40.249 --> 01:15:41.917
[both laughing]

01:15:42.668 --> 01:15:44.752
- What is it? Tuberculosis?
- You know what?

01:15:44.753 --> 01:15:49.299
They are doing just fine,
but they need to stay home.

01:15:50.926 --> 01:15:53.678
I had hoped to speak to them
in person because...

01:15:53.679 --> 01:15:56.139
[inhales] ...this is awkward,

01:15:56.682 --> 01:15:59.934
but a concerned individual has
lodged a welfare complaint.

01:15:59.935 --> 01:16:01.936
And unfortunately,
I need to make contact

01:16:01.937 --> 01:16:04.230
with the child's
legal guardian.

01:16:04.231 --> 01:16:06.607
It's something
that's not really negotiable.

01:16:06.608 --> 01:16:09.443
I need to speak
with their parents in person.

01:16:09.444 --> 01:16:10.945
Oh, dear.

01:16:10.946 --> 01:16:13.782
I could come over to the house
if that would make it easier.

01:16:14.575 --> 01:16:17.243
I'm just trying to avoid
involving CPS.

01:16:17.244 --> 01:16:18.870
- But frankly...
- CPS?

01:16:18.871 --> 01:16:21.080
...I'm not convinced
that anything is wrong.

01:16:21.081 --> 01:16:22.749
Who made the complaint?

01:16:23.500 --> 01:16:25.544
I'm not at liberty to say.

01:16:28.130 --> 01:16:30.047
Well, this is very upsetting.

01:16:30.048 --> 01:16:33.468
[TV] <i>It is now that
all free will has been lost.</i>

01:16:34.845 --> 01:16:36.721
<i>The ant moves
under the direction</i>

01:16:36.722 --> 01:16:39.099
<i>of a mind separate
from its own.</i>

01:16:41.268 --> 01:16:42.852
<i>Here, the ant initiates
its death grip.</i>

01:16:42.853 --> 01:16:44.687
Yum, yum, yum.

01:16:44.688 --> 01:16:45.814
There we go.

01:16:48.442 --> 01:16:52.737
<i>As the parasitic Cordyceps
continue to feed off its body.</i>

01:16:52.738 --> 01:16:54.281
That's disgusting.

01:16:57.868 --> 01:16:59.870
<i>Fungal fruiting occurs next.</i>

01:17:01.663 --> 01:17:03.206
<i>- Large blooms...</i>
- [doorbell rings]

01:17:03.207 --> 01:17:04.373
<i>...that serve
to spread more spores...</i>

01:17:04.374 --> 01:17:05.459
Who could that be?

01:17:08.086 --> 01:17:11.131
<i>...that will find more ants.</i>

01:17:11.757 --> 01:17:12.758
[man] Ew.

01:17:16.220 --> 01:17:18.387
[panting]

01:17:18.388 --> 01:17:20.307
- Thank God you're home.
- [man] Who is it?

01:17:21.141 --> 01:17:22.850
I'm so sorry to disturb you
on a Saturday.

01:17:22.851 --> 01:17:24.852
Oh, will you please,
please forgive me?

01:17:24.853 --> 01:17:26.229
We're just sitting down.

01:17:26.230 --> 01:17:28.898
The bus didn't pick me up
where it was scheduled to.

01:17:28.899 --> 01:17:30.900
And I had realized
far too late...

01:17:30.901 --> 01:17:32.318
[inhales]

01:17:32.319 --> 01:17:34.403
...that I was standing
on the wrong corner.

01:17:34.404 --> 01:17:35.905
And by the time
I put that together,

01:17:35.906 --> 01:17:38.574
oh, I'd missed it entirely.

01:17:38.575 --> 01:17:42.453
So I had to walk all the way
across town to get here.

01:17:42.454 --> 01:17:43.996
Well, I'm so sorry
to hear that...

01:17:43.997 --> 01:17:46.082
I am sorry to tell you this,
sweetie,

01:17:46.083 --> 01:17:48.668
but I am on the verge
of collapse.

01:17:48.669 --> 01:17:49.586
Oh.

01:17:51.755 --> 01:17:53.590
Could I please
have some water?

01:17:54.925 --> 01:17:55.925
I'm afraid that's re...

01:17:55.926 --> 01:17:58.219
Of course
you can have some water.

01:17:58.220 --> 01:17:59.512
Oh, thank you so much.

01:17:59.513 --> 01:18:00.972
I'm afraid
it's really not a...

01:18:00.973 --> 01:18:02.849
My name's Gladys,
it's so nice to meet you.

01:18:02.850 --> 01:18:03.934
Hi.

01:18:04.643 --> 01:18:08.229
Oh! I absolutely love
this house.

01:18:08.230 --> 01:18:11.148
Look, a giraffe
and a green Chinese la...

01:18:11.149 --> 01:18:13.276
That's original in there.
I bet it is.

01:18:13.277 --> 01:18:15.570
[clapping]
Oh, I just love this kitchen.

01:18:15.571 --> 01:18:19.156
Clean, white cabinets.
How I'm envious of that.

01:18:19.157 --> 01:18:20.284
[laughs]

01:18:20.993 --> 01:18:23.286
Now, listen.
I know that it's inconvenient,

01:18:23.287 --> 01:18:25.079
but I really needed
to speak to you

01:18:25.080 --> 01:18:27.081
about our conversation
yesterday.

01:18:27.082 --> 01:18:28.749
[coughs] Oh.

01:18:28.750 --> 01:18:29.709
[coughs]

01:18:29.710 --> 01:18:31.294
Marcus, get her a glass.

01:18:31.295 --> 01:18:33.046
A bowl, please.

01:18:35.132 --> 01:18:36.132
A bowl?

01:18:36.133 --> 01:18:38.718
Yes, a bowl.
It's a peculiarity of mine.

01:18:38.719 --> 01:18:40.888
I don't even try
to rationalize it anymore.

01:18:43.891 --> 01:18:46.767
A bowl of water. Okay.

01:18:46.768 --> 01:18:47.935
Thank you.

01:18:47.936 --> 01:18:50.479
I-I wanted you to know that
I talked to Alex's father,

01:18:50.480 --> 01:18:52.398
who's very ill, as I said.

01:18:52.399 --> 01:18:54.650
But the good news is,
he's more than happy

01:18:54.651 --> 01:18:57.153
to come in Monday,
sit down with you

01:18:57.154 --> 01:18:58.530
and clear everything up.

01:18:59.573 --> 01:19:02.491
I appreciate that,
but it really is unnecessary.

01:19:02.492 --> 01:19:04.911
So there's no need to contact
the authorities, right?

01:19:04.912 --> 01:19:05.829
That's, uh...

01:19:06.538 --> 01:19:07.830
Sure, I guess not.

01:19:07.831 --> 01:19:10.166
I mean, you haven't
contacted them yet, right?

01:19:10.167 --> 01:19:13.086
Gladys, I'm really gonna
have to insist that you, uh...

01:19:15.422 --> 01:19:17.132
Is... Is that my ribbon?

01:19:19.718 --> 01:19:21.929
You haven't
contacted them, right?

01:19:22.971 --> 01:19:24.806
No, I haven't. What is this?

01:19:27.392 --> 01:19:28.392
[man] Oh, my God!

01:19:28.393 --> 01:19:30.895
Whoops! Look what I did.
Oh, my goodness.

01:19:30.896 --> 01:19:32.522
Why did you do that?

01:19:32.523 --> 01:19:34.732
Well, it was an accident,
of course.

01:19:34.733 --> 01:19:36.943
Wow. That's really bleeding.

01:19:36.944 --> 01:19:38.110
Terry, go get the alcohol

01:19:38.111 --> 01:19:39.654
- and the first aid kit.
- Okay.

01:19:39.655 --> 01:19:42.073
Oh, no, no, no.
That's nonsense.

01:19:42.074 --> 01:19:44.659
Could you get me
a rag, sweetie?

01:19:44.660 --> 01:19:46.203
[stammering]

01:19:52.042 --> 01:19:53.210
[shrieks]

01:19:53.794 --> 01:19:54.877
I think she cut my hair!

01:19:54.878 --> 01:19:56.087
I'm calling 911.

01:19:56.088 --> 01:19:57.964
Marcus, I think
she cut my hair!

01:19:57.965 --> 01:20:00.342
Marcus, what did she do?

01:20:02.219 --> 01:20:03.387
[dings]

01:20:05.973 --> 01:20:07.391
[choking, panting]

01:20:11.812 --> 01:20:12.813
Marcus?

01:20:16.775 --> 01:20:17.776
Marcus?

01:20:28.120 --> 01:20:28.954
[gasps]

01:20:36.461 --> 01:20:38.088
[gurgling]

01:20:50.142 --> 01:20:51.393
- Well...
- [thudding]

01:20:54.396 --> 01:20:55.522
[groaning]

01:20:58.025 --> 01:20:59.693
- [Gladys humming]
- [thudding continues]

01:21:10.746 --> 01:21:12.748
[Marcus groaning and panting]

01:21:48.492 --> 01:21:49.493
[sighs]

01:22:04.675 --> 01:22:06.635
- [Marcus panting]
- [dog barking]

01:22:09.096 --> 01:22:10.137
[person on street] Look!

01:22:10.138 --> 01:22:11.223
[car tires screech,
horn honks]

01:22:12.474 --> 01:22:13.892
[person in park]
Yo, what the fuck, man?

01:22:15.769 --> 01:22:17.020
[people in park shouting]

01:22:17.771 --> 01:22:18.771
[person at table] Oh, my God.

01:22:18.772 --> 01:22:20.607
[panting continuing]

01:22:26.613 --> 01:22:28.406
[Archer] Come out with it.
Just think of the kids.

01:22:28.407 --> 01:22:30.074
- Stop thinking of yourself!
- [Justine] Marcus?

01:22:30.075 --> 01:22:31.993
- You and I are gonna have a...
- [Marcus snarling]

01:22:31.994 --> 01:22:33.495
- [Justine shrieking]
- [Marcus grunting]

01:22:37.499 --> 01:22:38.500
[Archer yells]

01:22:45.591 --> 01:22:46.967
[snarling]

01:22:49.720 --> 01:22:50.762
[Archer yells]

01:22:52.055 --> 01:22:53.056
[Archer] Stay down.

01:22:55.726 --> 01:22:57.144
Hey! Stop! No!

01:22:58.562 --> 01:23:00.354
Oh, my God. [whimpering]

01:23:00.355 --> 01:23:02.440
Help me, please. Please.

01:23:02.441 --> 01:23:04.233
Oh, God. No! [screams]

01:23:04.234 --> 01:23:05.819
- [whimpering]
- [door chimes]

01:23:09.448 --> 01:23:10.449
[shrieking]

01:23:11.575 --> 01:23:12.575
Oh, my God.

01:23:12.576 --> 01:23:14.703
[screaming]

01:23:18.457 --> 01:23:19.833
[shrieking]

01:23:20.876 --> 01:23:22.002
[Archer] Hey!

01:23:24.838 --> 01:23:25.838
Oh, my...

01:23:25.839 --> 01:23:27.299
[gasping]

01:23:30.010 --> 01:23:31.428
[whimpers, babbles]

01:23:34.973 --> 01:23:37.225
- Get out of my store!
- Fucking help me!

01:23:37.226 --> 01:23:39.061
[shrieking]

01:23:44.107 --> 01:23:45.608
- [Marcus growling]
- [screaming]

01:23:45.609 --> 01:23:47.778
[Marcus babbling]

01:23:49.154 --> 01:23:50.697
[snarling]

01:23:53.909 --> 01:23:55.202
[Justine screaming]

01:24:01.959 --> 01:24:03.043
What the fuck?

01:24:03.794 --> 01:24:05.170
[groaning]

01:24:09.883 --> 01:24:10.884
Motherfucker.

01:24:21.812 --> 01:24:23.814
Come on, you piece of shit.

01:24:29.111 --> 01:24:31.446
[muffled screaming]

01:24:37.160 --> 01:24:39.162
[screaming continuing]

01:24:41.290 --> 01:24:42.583
[woman screaming]

01:24:48.380 --> 01:24:49.589
[sound becomes clearer]

01:24:49.590 --> 01:24:52.301
[woman continues screaming]

01:24:54.261 --> 01:24:55.846
[low chattering]

01:25:02.728 --> 01:25:04.438
[no audible dialogue]

01:25:27.586 --> 01:25:28.587
Are you okay?

01:25:29.713 --> 01:25:31.673
Yeah, I think so.

01:25:32.466 --> 01:25:33.467
I'm just, uh...

01:25:34.593 --> 01:25:35.594
scraped up.

01:25:36.303 --> 01:25:37.304
You?

01:25:39.348 --> 01:25:40.349
The same.

01:25:41.850 --> 01:25:43.100
I-I wanna thank you.

01:25:43.101 --> 01:25:45.020
- Ah...
- No, I do. So, thank you.

01:25:47.439 --> 01:25:48.440
Sure.

01:25:48.982 --> 01:25:50.442
I mean, what else could I do?

01:25:53.195 --> 01:25:54.530
Guy was out of control.

01:25:55.447 --> 01:25:58.658
The last time I talked to him,
he was fine.

01:25:58.659 --> 01:26:00.202
I mean, he really was.

01:26:00.702 --> 01:26:01.703
[stammers]

01:26:02.329 --> 01:26:05.457
I've never seen anything
like that in my life.

01:26:06.500 --> 01:26:07.501
I have.

01:26:08.335 --> 01:26:09.670
What are you talking about?

01:26:11.046 --> 01:26:13.507
The way he was running,
I've seen that before.

01:26:17.553 --> 01:26:18.804
Can I show you something?

01:26:20.138 --> 01:26:23.015
Their little girl ran
the same way Matthew did.

01:26:23.016 --> 01:26:25.351
Same posture, same exact way.

01:26:25.352 --> 01:26:28.187
Just like Marcus
ran after you today.

01:26:28.188 --> 01:26:29.647
He was weaponized.

01:26:29.648 --> 01:26:32.901
Like a heat-seeking missile
just locked onto you.

01:26:33.694 --> 01:26:36.320
So, here. Look at this.
This is my house.

01:26:36.321 --> 01:26:37.989
This is Bailey Kramer's house.

01:26:37.990 --> 01:26:40.199
Now, if you assume they were
heading in a straight line

01:26:40.200 --> 01:26:42.285
at just some target of theirs,

01:26:42.286 --> 01:26:44.662
and you assume they both had
the same target,

01:26:44.663 --> 01:26:47.331
those lines intersect
somewhere around here.

01:26:47.332 --> 01:26:48.249
Oh, my God.

01:26:48.250 --> 01:26:49.709
There must be something
about this area.

01:26:49.710 --> 01:26:52.004
- Alex.
- Some-- What?

01:26:52.713 --> 01:26:55.090
Alex Lilly lives
in this house.

01:27:01.054 --> 01:27:04.224
Who else can think
of an example of a parasite?

01:27:04.766 --> 01:27:05.767
Anyone?

01:27:06.727 --> 01:27:08.477
- Lisa?
- A tapeworm.

01:27:08.478 --> 01:27:10.771
A tapeworm! Very good!

01:27:10.772 --> 01:27:12.440
That's a gross one, right?

01:27:12.441 --> 01:27:16.068
It lives in your intestines
and it eats your food.

01:27:16.069 --> 01:27:17.487
[children chattering]

01:27:20.657 --> 01:27:21.866
Stop it.

01:27:21.867 --> 01:27:22.951
"Stop it."

01:27:24.369 --> 01:27:26.662
- "Stop it."
- [other children laughing]

01:27:26.663 --> 01:27:27.789
"Stop it."

01:27:29.041 --> 01:27:30.083
"Stop it."

01:27:38.258 --> 01:27:40.177
[children chatter, shout]

01:27:46.558 --> 01:27:47.726
[man] What's up, Axe Man?

01:27:50.687 --> 01:27:53.023
Talk to me, Axe Man.
How was school today?

01:27:53.941 --> 01:27:56.442
- Good.
- Good? Kiss any supermodels?

01:27:56.443 --> 01:27:57.985
[chuckles] No.

01:27:57.986 --> 01:27:59.738
No? All right.

01:28:01.448 --> 01:28:03.492
Well,
tonight's the night, pal.

01:28:04.076 --> 01:28:06.537
Your mom's aunt Gladys
is coming, remember?

01:28:07.496 --> 01:28:10.499
[sighs] Why do we have to
have her live at our house?

01:28:11.124 --> 01:28:13.126
'Cause it's like
we talked about.

01:28:13.710 --> 01:28:17.673
She's sick, and she doesn't
have anywhere else to go.

01:28:19.424 --> 01:28:21.425
But I don't even
know her, though.

01:28:21.426 --> 01:28:24.096
Pfft. I hear you, bud.
I don't know her either.

01:28:24.805 --> 01:28:27.682
To be honest, I'm not sure
your mom knows her that well.

01:28:27.683 --> 01:28:31.144
But she's family.
Family's important.

01:28:32.062 --> 01:28:33.605
We gotta help each other out.

01:28:34.314 --> 01:28:35.899
Hey, found a kid.

01:28:36.400 --> 01:28:39.527
Hey. My men have returned.

01:28:39.528 --> 01:28:40.611
- Hi.
- Hi.

01:28:40.612 --> 01:28:42.780
Whoa. Hey. Good day at school?

01:28:42.781 --> 01:28:44.448
- Yeah.
- Okay, good.

01:28:44.449 --> 01:28:47.118
Uh, I would really like to
get this house cleaned up

01:28:47.119 --> 01:28:48.744
before your aunt Gladys
gets here.

01:28:48.745 --> 01:28:50.496
So do me a favor,
get your room cleaned up

01:28:50.497 --> 01:28:52.123
before you start
your homework.

01:28:52.124 --> 01:28:54.168
She's not coming in my room,
is she?

01:28:54.918 --> 01:28:56.169
I'd really like a clean house.

01:28:56.170 --> 01:28:58.463
That includes your room,
so let's go.

01:28:59.423 --> 01:29:02.676
I know. It's horrible
cleaning up after yourself.

01:29:12.978 --> 01:29:14.938
[car doors shutting]

01:29:30.329 --> 01:29:31.538
[dad] All right?

01:29:38.212 --> 01:29:40.129
[mom] Hi! Come in!

01:29:40.130 --> 01:29:42.173
- [dad] Got the door?
- [mom] I got it.

01:29:42.174 --> 01:29:44.092
[dad] One more step.

01:29:55.771 --> 01:29:58.439
[dad] I'm just saying
she looks really bad.

01:29:58.440 --> 01:29:59.774
I don't know if this
is the place for...

01:29:59.775 --> 01:30:02.151
Yeah, well, it's either here
or out on the street, Stephen.

01:30:02.152 --> 01:30:05.738
Well, you know, this ain't
a hospice place, hon.

01:30:05.739 --> 01:30:06.864
I know that. I know.

01:30:06.865 --> 01:30:08.824
We're not equipped for this
kind of thing. All right?

01:30:08.825 --> 01:30:11.118
We hadn't seen this woman
in 15 years.

01:30:11.119 --> 01:30:12.620
She didn't even show up
to our wedding...

01:30:12.621 --> 01:30:13.996
Look, my mom
would do this for her,

01:30:13.997 --> 01:30:16.374
so I'm gonna do this
for her, okay?

01:30:16.375 --> 01:30:17.708
I could really
use your support.

01:30:17.709 --> 01:30:19.002
If at any point
you feel like...

01:30:19.545 --> 01:30:21.587
Alex, honey,
what are you doing?

01:30:21.588 --> 01:30:22.713
I'm hungry.

01:30:22.714 --> 01:30:24.382
Oh, you're hungry.
Okay. All right.

01:30:24.383 --> 01:30:25.633
Well, go downstairs, eat up

01:30:25.634 --> 01:30:28.344
and then go brush your teeth,
okay? It's almost 7:30.

01:30:28.345 --> 01:30:31.056
And be quiet back there.
Your aunt Gladys is sleeping.

01:30:56.665 --> 01:30:57.666
[door creaks]

01:31:08.552 --> 01:31:10.012
[door creaking]

01:31:21.315 --> 01:31:22.149
[gasps]

01:31:24.484 --> 01:31:26.612
How long
is she gonna stay with us?

01:31:29.072 --> 01:31:30.532
Hard to say, pal.

01:31:31.617 --> 01:31:33.785
Doesn't look like
she's getting much better.

01:31:35.078 --> 01:31:37.288
So she's gonna stay
with us forever?

01:31:37.289 --> 01:31:38.623
No.

01:31:38.624 --> 01:31:39.749
I...

01:31:39.750 --> 01:31:41.960
I don't think she'll be here
longer than a month.

01:31:47.883 --> 01:31:49.343
[children chattering]

01:31:55.933 --> 01:31:57.850
- All righty, man.
- All righty.

01:31:57.851 --> 01:31:59.101
I'll pick you up
at 2:00, okay?

01:31:59.102 --> 01:32:00.853
- See ya.
- See ya.

01:32:00.854 --> 01:32:02.606
- I love you.
- Love ya.

01:32:06.568 --> 01:32:08.529
[Justine] That's time.
Pencils down.

01:32:09.863 --> 01:32:11.113
Matthew!

01:32:11.114 --> 01:32:12.448
What?
You said, "Pencils down."

01:32:12.449 --> 01:32:14.158
Matthew, outside now.

01:32:14.159 --> 01:32:15.451
Alex, are you okay?

01:32:15.452 --> 01:32:16.911
I'm fine.

01:32:16.912 --> 01:32:19.206
Matthew, let's go.
Get your bag.

01:32:19.957 --> 01:32:22.209
It was a joke. Oh, my God!

01:32:23.335 --> 01:32:24.962
- [bell ringing]
- [students chattering]

01:32:43.605 --> 01:32:45.731
- You miss your ride, son?
- I'm okay.

01:32:45.732 --> 01:32:46.817
You sure?

01:33:36.033 --> 01:33:40.746
Mom, Dad, where were you?

01:33:41.830 --> 01:33:44.917
Hey, Axe Man. How was school?

01:33:46.251 --> 01:33:47.252
What's wrong?

01:33:48.003 --> 01:33:49.171
Alex?

01:33:49.963 --> 01:33:52.089
Oh, welcome home.

01:33:52.090 --> 01:33:53.049
[chuckles]

01:33:53.050 --> 01:33:54.676
How are you, sweetie?

01:33:57.179 --> 01:33:58.596
Let me take a look at you.

01:33:58.597 --> 01:33:59.680
Oh, you know,
I haven't seen you

01:33:59.681 --> 01:34:01.807
since you were
a little teeny baby.

01:34:01.808 --> 01:34:03.226
What's wrong with my parents?

01:34:03.227 --> 01:34:05.853
Oh, nothing, sweetheart.
They're just fine.

01:34:05.854 --> 01:34:07.189
Mom.

01:34:09.024 --> 01:34:11.984
Hey. How was school?

01:34:11.985 --> 01:34:14.863
You see? I told you,
she's just fine. Don't worry.

01:34:17.115 --> 01:34:18.116
Alex.

01:34:19.201 --> 01:34:20.494
Now, don't be rude.

01:34:21.745 --> 01:34:23.162
Why don't you sit down
at the table?

01:34:23.163 --> 01:34:24.830
'Cause I'm making dinner.
I should have asked you,

01:34:24.831 --> 01:34:25.998
but you weren't here,

01:34:25.999 --> 01:34:27.793
so I thought mac and cheese
would...

01:34:28.585 --> 01:34:29.752
Dad!

01:34:29.753 --> 01:34:32.004
Alex, that's it.

01:34:32.005 --> 01:34:34.257
I want you to go upstairs,
wash your face,

01:34:34.258 --> 01:34:35.925
brush your teeth,
and then it is bedtime.

01:34:35.926 --> 01:34:37.052
No dinner for you.

01:34:40.430 --> 01:34:41.974
I'm not kidding, young man.
Go.

01:35:19.178 --> 01:35:20.679
Come. Sit.

01:35:30.856 --> 01:35:31.857
Alex.

01:35:32.524 --> 01:35:33.567
Sit.

01:35:39.364 --> 01:35:41.032
Don't worry about
your parents.

01:35:41.033 --> 01:35:42.409
They're just resting.

01:35:46.663 --> 01:35:49.999
Now, before you go to school
today, I want you to promise

01:35:50.000 --> 01:35:53.212
that you will not tell
a living soul that I am here

01:35:54.213 --> 01:35:56.548
or that your parents
are resting like they are.

01:36:00.177 --> 01:36:01.428
Do you hear me, Alex?

01:36:08.352 --> 01:36:09.353
Watch.

01:36:12.147 --> 01:36:13.232
Ooh.

01:36:23.534 --> 01:36:24.910
Are you watching?

01:36:36.255 --> 01:36:37.548
Stop!

01:36:38.632 --> 01:36:39.800
Stop, Dad!

01:36:42.261 --> 01:36:43.428
Alex.

01:36:52.604 --> 01:36:53.647
Sit down.

01:37:05.284 --> 01:37:07.493
Now, when I tell you
that you are not to speak

01:37:07.494 --> 01:37:10.455
about me or your parents
to anyone...

01:37:12.082 --> 01:37:15.377
you understand what can happen
if you break your promise.

01:37:18.714 --> 01:37:20.464
I can make your parents
hurt themselves.

01:37:20.465 --> 01:37:22.467
I can make them
hurt each other.

01:37:25.721 --> 01:37:28.515
I can make them eat each other
if I want to.

01:37:32.352 --> 01:37:34.021
Do I want to, Alex?

01:37:36.648 --> 01:37:38.066
Do you believe me?

01:37:42.237 --> 01:37:43.571
Promise you will not
talk about me

01:37:43.572 --> 01:37:45.991
to another human being.
Say it.

01:37:47.451 --> 01:37:48.577
I promise.

01:37:50.329 --> 01:37:51.705
'Cause I'll know, Alex.

01:37:54.917 --> 01:37:56.668
Go to school. Take the bus.

01:38:56.353 --> 01:38:57.729
No talking today.

01:38:59.398 --> 01:39:00.399
Good boy.

01:39:01.859 --> 01:39:03.150
You'll need to
feed your parents.

01:39:03.151 --> 01:39:04.653
There's soup in the cabinet.

01:39:06.822 --> 01:39:08.490
Tomorrow,
you'll get some more.

01:39:29.052 --> 01:39:30.596
[students shouting,
chattering]

01:39:53.827 --> 01:39:54.995
[Gladys, distant] Alex.

01:39:59.625 --> 01:40:00.626
Alex?

01:40:23.649 --> 01:40:24.942
Come here, sweetie.

01:40:26.026 --> 01:40:27.694
[labored breathing]

01:40:31.573 --> 01:40:32.616
Oh.

01:40:36.328 --> 01:40:38.038
I'm very sick, Alex.

01:40:40.374 --> 01:40:42.125
Would you like some water?

01:40:42.960 --> 01:40:44.545
Well, water won't help me.

01:40:45.671 --> 01:40:47.381
I'm too sick for water.

01:40:48.590 --> 01:40:50.759
I have been
for a very long time.

01:40:52.469 --> 01:40:53.929
What will make you better?

01:40:56.723 --> 01:40:58.349
Well, I was hoping
your mom and dad

01:40:58.350 --> 01:40:59.642
would make me feel better,

01:40:59.643 --> 01:41:02.396
but it doesn't seem to be
turning out so good.

01:41:03.105 --> 01:41:05.190
Would you like to go
to a hospital?

01:41:05.983 --> 01:41:08.068
Hospital won't fix me.

01:41:13.657 --> 01:41:15.116
But maybe you could, though.

01:41:15.117 --> 01:41:16.493
You could help.

01:41:17.369 --> 01:41:18.370
How?

01:41:19.246 --> 01:41:20.414
Well, at school,

01:41:21.582 --> 01:41:25.085
bring an object from each
of your classmates home to me.

01:41:26.170 --> 01:41:27.337
That might work.

01:41:28.714 --> 01:41:30.299
How will that make you better?

01:41:34.011 --> 01:41:36.138
It might be just what I need.

01:41:39.308 --> 01:41:41.810
And if you got better,
you'd go back home?

01:41:45.772 --> 01:41:47.274
If I got better...

01:41:49.610 --> 01:41:51.028
I'd go back home.

01:41:54.281 --> 01:41:55.365
[laughs]

01:42:52.005 --> 01:42:53.006
Alex.

01:42:54.967 --> 01:42:56.509
What are you doing in here?

01:42:56.510 --> 01:42:59.136
Um, I didn't
feel like playing,

01:42:59.137 --> 01:43:01.223
and I forgot something.

01:43:02.641 --> 01:43:04.601
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hey, hey, hey.

01:43:08.063 --> 01:43:09.064
Are you okay?

01:43:09.690 --> 01:43:11.149
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

01:43:12.109 --> 01:43:14.778
You've been
awful quiet lately.

01:43:15.445 --> 01:43:16.613
Quieter than usual.

01:43:17.281 --> 01:43:18.323
How are you doing?

01:43:18.866 --> 01:43:21.326
I'm okay.
I just forgot something.

01:43:22.244 --> 01:43:23.245
It's okay.

01:43:25.372 --> 01:43:26.831
Alex, you know,

01:43:26.832 --> 01:43:29.543
if... you ever want to talk
to someone,

01:43:30.043 --> 01:43:31.461
you can always talk to me.

01:43:33.046 --> 01:43:34.255
Do you know that?

01:43:34.256 --> 01:43:35.423
Yeah.

01:43:35.424 --> 01:43:37.759
You can talk to me
about anything you want.

01:43:41.263 --> 01:43:42.639
I wanna go back now.

01:43:44.558 --> 01:43:46.518
Okay. Go play.

01:44:22.012 --> 01:44:23.138
[clanking]

01:44:24.681 --> 01:44:26.350
[scraping, muffled speech]

01:44:27.601 --> 01:44:29.228
[noise continuing]

01:44:43.825 --> 01:44:45.077
What are you doing?

01:45:07.891 --> 01:45:09.059
[rings]

01:46:31.892 --> 01:46:33.142
[Justine laughing]

01:46:33.143 --> 01:46:34.228
No...

01:46:44.029 --> 01:46:46.280
[Gladys] <i>Stephen here suffered
a stroke a little while back,</i>

01:46:46.281 --> 01:46:48.157
<i>so he's unable to speak.</i>

01:46:48.158 --> 01:46:50.827
<i>And I'm taking care of
the family for the time being.</i>

01:46:51.328 --> 01:46:53.037
I'm glad you both are here.

01:46:53.038 --> 01:46:55.248
Alex, how are you doing, pal?

01:46:55.249 --> 01:46:56.582
I'm okay.

01:46:56.583 --> 01:46:58.209
Now, we're gonna ask you
some questions

01:46:58.210 --> 01:47:00.128
about what happened
at school, okay?

01:47:02.464 --> 01:47:04.299
Tomorrow,
people will come here.

01:47:05.926 --> 01:47:07.845
And they will search
this house...

01:47:12.516 --> 01:47:14.309
and we have to be ready.

01:47:31.994 --> 01:47:33.661
[doorbell rings]

01:47:33.662 --> 01:47:35.204
Detective, come in!

01:47:35.205 --> 01:47:36.289
Good morning, Ms. Lilly.

01:47:36.290 --> 01:47:37.540
- How are you today?
- Fine.

01:47:37.541 --> 01:47:39.375
- Good to see you again.
- Nice to see you too.

01:47:39.376 --> 01:47:41.085
- Remember Detective Colbert?
- Oh, yes.

01:47:41.086 --> 01:47:43.546
We just wanted to come by the
house for a few minutes today

01:47:43.547 --> 01:47:44.839
and look around, uh,

01:47:44.840 --> 01:47:47.800
see the environment
that Alex has been living in.

01:47:47.801 --> 01:47:51.345
And just get an idea of what
the family dynamic is like.

01:47:51.346 --> 01:47:53.598
- Okay!
- Oh. Thank you.

01:47:53.599 --> 01:47:54.682
And... Oh.

01:47:54.683 --> 01:47:56.602
Hey, Alex.
How are you doing today?

01:47:57.644 --> 01:47:58.895
He's a little quiet today, right?

01:47:58.896 --> 01:48:00.689
- Mm-hmm. Yes, he is.
- Okay.

01:49:05.128 --> 01:49:06.213
Hello?

01:49:15.013 --> 01:49:17.182
Pack your things, Alex,
we're leaving tomorrow.

01:49:20.352 --> 01:49:21.979
Don't step over the salt.

01:49:54.970 --> 01:49:57.389
The cops are here.
What do you think that means?

01:49:59.766 --> 01:50:00.809
I don't know.

01:50:02.144 --> 01:50:03.561
Do we knock? Do we come back?

01:50:03.562 --> 01:50:05.105
Maybe we knock.

01:50:05.606 --> 01:50:08.317
And say what? What...
What are we gonna explain?

01:50:11.320 --> 01:50:12.195
Yeah, I don't know.

01:50:12.196 --> 01:50:13.322
- Let's just...
- Here we go.

01:50:14.948 --> 01:50:16.158
Hey, what is this?

01:50:29.171 --> 01:50:30.214
Is that the cop?

01:50:31.548 --> 01:50:33.049
That's Paul.

01:50:33.050 --> 01:50:35.093
- You know him?
- Yeah.

01:51:07.042 --> 01:51:08.627
[creaking]

01:51:15.676 --> 01:51:16.677
Hello?

01:51:31.859 --> 01:51:32.860
Paul?

01:51:46.206 --> 01:51:48.708
[voice trembling] Paul,
what are you doing back there?

01:51:48.709 --> 01:51:49.625
[Archer] Wait.

01:51:49.626 --> 01:51:51.419
[James screeching]

01:51:51.420 --> 01:51:53.922
- [Paul screeching]
- [Justine screams]

01:51:55.382 --> 01:51:57.009
[muffled shouting]

01:52:01.054 --> 01:52:02.556
- [Justine screaming]
- [Archer shouting]

01:52:03.348 --> 01:52:05.726
- [thudding]
- [Justine screaming]

01:52:10.063 --> 01:52:12.149
